<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Akhulgo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasian-war">Caucasian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The siege of Akhulgo was a Russian siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Imam Shamil</a>'s mountain fortress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a> in the summer of 1839. A Russian force under General Pavel Grabbe stormed the fortress in August after some eighty days, at a heavy cost on both sides, and most of the defenders and their families died. Shamil escaped and rebuilt his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a>.</p></div>
